# Yesterday's buses, on a day that has none of its own.
#
# GTFS counts `arrival_time` from the start of the service day and lets it run
# past 24:00. A trip at 24:39 is one you catch at 00:39 the next morning, and it
# belongs to the previous service day, not to the one the clock says.
#
# 2026-09-12 is a Saturday. The bus service in this slice runs Fridays and the
# rail service runs weekdays, so Saturday has no service of its own. Everything
# on this board therefore comes from Friday, shifted back across midnight.
#
# Three things have to be right at once for a row to appear here. The app has to
# consult yesterday's services. It has to carry yesterday's window into the
# query. And it has to mark the trip as belonging to a day that has ended, which
# is what stops a 24:39 departure from reading as a quarter past one in the
# afternoon.
#
# None of that was reachable before: the slice topped out at 23:25, so nothing
# it held could cross midnight.
cache ../cache.db
date 2026-09-12
time 00:00
offset -04:00
size 100 14

# A pin is the way in. Searching cannot reach this board: `search_stops` asks
# which stops have service *today*, and today has none, so it finds nothing
# while a bus is four minutes away. The pin resolves by stop id instead.
enter
